WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Add heat →
Heating moves the rock rightward. Intergranular melt appears only after the solidus is crossed.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Reduce pressure ↑
Rising rock moves upward on the pressure axis. Its temperature can stay nearly constant as melting begins.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Add water → lower the solidus
Adding water shifts the solidus left. The sample can begin melting without getting hotter.
